package instructions

// OverviewMarker identifies the overview document returned for unknown topics.
const OverviewMarker = "# Langflow Quick Reference"

// LangflowInstructions contains the comprehensive LLM guidance text for working with Langflow.
// This is used by the langflow_concepts tool to provide quick reference documentation.
const LangflowInstructions = OverviewMarker + "\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### Components\nLangflow components are the building blocks of flows. Each component has:\n- **Inputs**: Configuration fields (template fields) that accept values or connections\n- **Outputs**: Data outputs that can connect to other components' inputs\n- **Base Classes**: Categories like \"Tool\", \"Memory\", \"Model\", \"VectorStore\", etc.\n\n### Tool Mode\nWhen a component has tool_mode enabled:\n- Its outputs are replaced with a single \"component_as_tool\" output (type: Tool)\n- The component becomes callable by an Agent via its tools input\n- Fields marked tool_mode=true become tool parameters (provided by Agent at call time)\n- Fields marked tool_mode=false remain as configuration\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Enable tool_mode using the set_tool_mode tool, NOT update_node. The server must transform outputs.\n\n### Flow Execution\n- Adding/updating nodes does NOT execute them\n- Connecting nodes does NOT execute them\n- Use build_flow to execute the entire flow\n- Use build_node to execute a single component\n- Template components (prompts) need building to process templates\n\n### Connections\n- Connections are validated for type compatibility\n- Only the selected output type flows through connections\n- Hidden fields (show=false) cannot receive connections\n- Tool mode fields on tool_mode-enabled nodes have connections removed automatically\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Creating a Flow\n1. create_flow\n2. add_node for each component (use tool_mode=true for Agent tools)\n3. connect_nodes to wire components\n4. build_flow to execute\n\n### Using Components as Agent Tools\n1. Add component with add_node(tool_mode=true) or add_custom_component(code, tool_mode=true)\n2. Connect component's \"component_as_tool\" output to Agent's \"tools\" input\n3. build_flow\n\n### Custom Components (No Restart!)\nUse add_custom_component with inline Python code. The component works immediately:\n- No file creation needed\n- No server restart needed\n- Code is stored on the node (portable with flow)\n- tool_mode can be enabled in the same call\n\nExample:\n```python\nfrom langflow.custom import Component\nfrom langflow.io import MessageTextInput, Output\nfrom langflow.schema.message import Message\n\nclass MyComponent(Component):\n    display_name = \"My Component\"\n    description = \"What this does\"\n\n    inputs = [\n        MessageTextInput(name=\"input_text\", display_name=\"Input\"),\n    ]\n\n    outputs = [\n        Output(display_name=\"Result\", name=\"result\", method=\"process\"),\n    ]\n\n    def process(self) -> Message:\n        return Message(text=self.input_text.upper())\n```\n\n## Common Mistakes to Avoid\n\n1. **Retrying schema tools when poisoned** -- Use /api/v1/all dump instead\n2. **Using display names as component_type** -- Use exact types like \"LanguageModelComponent\", not \"Language Model\"\n3. **Trusting connect_nodes response** -- Always verify edges count after connecting\n4. **Using update_node for tool_mode** -- Use set_tool_mode instead\n5. **Assuming data persists in volumes** -- DB is in container layer\n6. **Blind PATCH to flows** -- GET -> mutate -> PATCH (body replaces entire data)\n\n## Layout Best Practices\n\n### Critical: Connection Line Rendering\nLangflow uses Bezier curves:\n- Exit: right edge of source + 7px, at output handle Y\n- Entry: left edge of target - 7px, at input handle Y\n- Curve bulges horizontally at midpoint\n\n### Spacing Rules\n- **Horizontal gap**: 600-1000px between connected nodes (node width = 384px)\n- **Vertical gap**: 600-800px when stacking nodes\n- **Branch lanes**: 800-1200px apart vertically\n- **Supporting nodes**: 600-800px above/below main flow\n- **Canvas**: 4000-8000px wide, 3000-6000px tall is fine\n\n### Layout Process\n1. analyze_flow_layout to understand structure\n2. Identify main path (longest input->output chain)\n3. Position main path horizontally at y=1500, x increasing by 800-1000px\n4. Position supporting nodes 600-800px above/below their consumers\n5. Position parallel branches in separate vertical lanes\n6. Verify no node covers connection lines\n\n## Available Concept Topics\n\n- custom_components -- Creating custom components with inline code\n- tool_mode -- How tool_mode works for making components callable by Agents\n- building -- How flow building/execution works\n- component_structure -- Basic component class structure\n- outputs -- How component outputs work\n- inputs -- How component inputs and fields work\n- connections -- How connections work and validation rules\n- common_mistakes -- Common mistakes to avoid (READ THIS!)\n- layout -- Layout best practices and spacing rules\n\n## Preconfigured Models\nLangflow has OpenAI Compatible provider with free models:\n- nemotron-3-ultra-free\n- nemotron-3.5-lightning-free\n- x-preview-f-free\n- muse-spark-1.2-contributor-free\n\nUse LanguageModelComponent with provider=\"OpenAI Compatible\" and model_name from above.\n"

// GetConcept returns the documentation for a specific concept topic.
func GetConcept(topic string) string {
	concepts := map[string]string{
		"custom_components":   "## Custom Components\n\nCreate custom components using inline Python code via add_custom_component.\n\n**Key Points:**\n- NO RESTART NEEDED -- code is evaluated dynamically by Langflow API\n- Code is stored on the node itself (portable with the flow)\n- Use tool_mode=true in add_custom_component to enable as Agent tool\n- The Component subclass defines inputs, outputs, and processing logic\n\n**Component Structure:**\n```python\nfrom langflow.custom import Component\nfrom langflow.io import MessageTextInput, Output\nfrom langflow.schema.message import Message\n\nclass MyComponent(Component):\n    display_name = \"My Component\"\n    description = \"What this does\"\n    icon = \"custom\"\n\n    inputs = [\n        MessageTextInput(name=\"input_text\", display_name=\"Input\", required=True),\n    ]\n\n    outputs = [\n        Output(display_name=\"Result\", name=\"result\", method=\"process\"),\n    ]\n\n    def process(self) -> Message:\n        return Message(text=self.input_text.upper())\n```\n\n**Input Types (langflow.io):**\n- MessageTextInput, MessageFileInput, MessageDataInput\n- IntInput, FloatInput, BoolInput, DropdownInput\n- HandleInput (connection-only), SecretStrInput\n- DataInput, DataFrameInput, VectorStoreInput\n\n**Output Types:**\n- Output(display_name, name, method) -- method is the function to call\n- Returns: Message, Data, DataFrame, list, dict, str, int, float, bool",
		"tool_mode":           "## Tool Mode\n\nTool mode transforms a component into an Agent-callable tool.\n\n**How It Works:**\n1. Call set_tool_mode(flow_id, node_id, enabled=true)\n2. Server transforms the node:\n   - Replaces all outputs with \"component_as_tool\" (type: Tool)\n   - Adds \"tools_metadata\" template field for tool config\n   - Updates base_classes to [\"Tool\"]\n3. Connect \"component_as_tool\" output to Agent's \"tools\" input\n\n**Field Behavior:**\n- Fields with tool_mode=true -> become tool parameters (Agent provides at call time)\n- Fields with tool_mode=false -> remain as configuration (set once at design time)\n- Connections to tool_mode=true fields are REMOVED when tool_mode is enabled\n\n**Using Existing Components as Tools:**\nMost built-in components already have tool_mode fields defined:\n1. add_node(component_type, tool_mode=true)\n2. Connect component_as_tool -> Agent.tools\n3. build_flow\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Use set_tool_mode tool, NOT update_node with tool_mode config.",
		"building":            "## Building & Execution\n\n**Critical:** Adding/updating/connecting nodes does NOT execute them!\n\n**Execution Methods:**\n- build_flow(flow_id) -- Execute entire flow, returns all component outputs\n- build_flow(flow_id, wait_for_completion=false) -- Returns job_id for polling\n- build_node(flow_id, node_id) -- Execute single component (dependencies must be built)\n- GetBuildStatus(job_id) -- Poll for async build results\n\n**Template Components:**\nPrompts and other template components need building to process their templates.\n\n**Build Process:**\n1. Resolves component dependencies\n2. Executes in topological order\n3. Passes data through connections\n4. Produces final outputs\n\n**After Changes:**\nALWAYS call build_flow to verify changes took effect and outputs are correct.",
		"component_structure": "## Component Structure\n\nA Langflow Component has:\n- **display_name**: UI display name\n- **description**: What the component does\n- **icon**: Icon identifier\n- **inputs**: List of input fields (TemplateField)\n- **outputs**: List of output fields (Output)\n- **Methods**: Functions that generate outputs\n\n**Base Classes (categories):**\n- Tool -- callable by Agents\n- Memory -- conversation memory\n- Model -- LLM/embedding models\n- VectorStore -- vector databases\n- Embedding -- embedding models\n- DocumentLoader -- document loading\n- TextSplitter -- text chunking\n- Retriever -- document retrieval\n- Chain -- LLM chains\n- Agent -- autonomous agents\n- Prompt -- prompt templates",
		"outputs":             "## Component Outputs\n\nOutputs define what data a component produces.\n\n**OutputField:**\n- types: List of type strings (e.g., [\"Message\", \"Data\"])\n- selected: Currently active type (only this type flows through connections)\n- name: Internal output name\n- display_name: UI display name\n- method: Component method that generates this output\n\n**Selected Output:**\n- Only the selected output type flows through connections\n- When connecting, use the output's current selected type\n- If connection fails, check if output type matches input's accepted types\n\n**Multiple Outputs:**\nComponents can have multiple outputs, but only one is \"selected\" at a time.",
		"inputs":              "## Component Inputs & Fields\n\n**TemplateField Properties:**\n- type: Field type (str, int, float, bool, etc.)\n- required: Whether field is mandatory\n- show: Whether field is visible in UI (show=false = cannot receive connections)\n- advanced: Show in advanced section\n- multiline: Multi-line text input\n- value: Default/configured value\n- name: Internal field name\n- display_name: UI label\n- info: Tooltip/help text\n- options: List of options for dropdown\n- input_types: Accepted connection types\n- tool_mode: When true, field becomes tool parameter (Agent provides at call time)\n\n**Connection Handling:**\n- Inputs accept values via: direct configuration OR incoming connection\n- Connection overrides configured value\n- HandleInput fields are \"connection only\" -- cannot be configured directly\n- Hidden fields (show=false) cannot receive connections",
		"connections":         "## Connections\n\n**Validation:**\n- Source output type must be compatible with target input's accepted types\n- Use ValidateConnection tool to check before connecting\n- Types are checked: output selected type vs input input_types\n\n**Automatic Removal:**\nConnections are automatically removed when flow loads if:\n- Target field is hidden (show=false)\n- Target node has tool_mode enabled AND target field has tool_mode=true\n- Types become incompatible\n\n**Edge Structure:**\n- source: source node ID\n- target: target node ID\n- sourceHandle: output name on source\n- targetHandle: input name on target\n- id: unique edge ID\n\n**Verify After Connecting:**\nAlways verify edges count after connect_nodes to catch silent edge loss.",
		"common_mistakes":     "## Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Reality |\n|---------|---------|\n| Retrying search_components when poisoned | Always crashes; use /api/v1/all dump instead |\n| Using display names as component_type | Use exact: \"LanguageModelComponent\" not \"Language Model\" |\n| Trusting connect_nodes OK response | Verify saved edges count via GET /api/v1/flows/{id} |\n| update_node with tool_mode config | Use set_tool_mode tool for server-side transformation |\n| Assuming data persists in volumes | DB is in container layer; export flows regularly |\n| Blind PATCH /api/v1/flows/{id} | Body replaces entire data; GET -> mutate -> PATCH |\n| JSON body to /api/v1/login | Must be form-encoded (application/x-www-form-urlencoded) |\n| Not building after changes | Changes don't take effect until build_flow runs |\n| Connecting to hidden fields | show=false fields cannot receive connections |\n| Not checking selected output type | Only selected output flows through connections |",
		"layout":              "## Layout Best Practices\n\n### Connection Line Rendering\nLangflow uses Bezier curves:\n- Exit: source.x + source.width + 7, at output handle Y\n- Entry: target.x - 7, at input handle Y\n- Control points at X midpoint, horizontal from source then to target\n- Line bulges HORIZONTALLY at midpoint\n\n### Spacing Rules (CRITICAL)\n- Node width: 384px (fixed)\n- Node height: 400-700px (check analyze_flow_layout!)\n- **Horizontal gap**: 600-1000px between connected nodes\n- **Vertical gap**: 600-800px when stacking\n- **Branch lanes**: 800-1200px vertical separation\n- **Supporting nodes**: 600-800px above/below main flow\n- **Canvas**: 4000-8000px wide, 3000-6000px tall\n\n### Layout Process\n1. analyze_flow_layout -> get node dimensions, connections, categories\n2. Identify main path (longest input->output chain)\n3. Position main path horizontally at y=1500, x += 800-1000 each\n4. Supporting nodes (models, tools) 600-800px above/below\n5. Parallel branches in separate lanes 800-1200px apart\n6. Check: no node in Y band between source/target at intermediate X\n7. If node covers line, move it UP or DOWN outside line's Y range\n\n### Example Layout\nMain: ChatInput -> Agent -> ChatOutput\n- ChatInput: (100, 1500)\n- Agent: (1000, 1500) -- 900px gap\n- ChatOutput: (2000, 1500) -- 1000px gap\n\nModel feeding Agent:\n- OpenAIModel: (800, 700) -- 800px above, slightly left\n\nTools:\n- Tool1: (600, 2300) -- 800px below Agent\n- Tool2: (600, 3000) -- 700px below Tool1\n- Both connect to Agent at (1000, 1500)",
	}

	if content, ok := concepts[topic]; ok {
		return content
	}

	// Return overview with all topics
	return LangflowInstructions
}
